that H4-T5 lacked. The earlier Heisenberg-Nil rule `dc=ab` is now classified
as an interaction-bearing local prototype, not as the literal global q79
topology.

The result also locates the missing nonlinear data. Since the topology-only
factor has no transferred higher products, physical vertices cannot be
attributed to the bare q79 circle topology. They must arise from at least one
of:

1. the twisted visible/hidden bundle and superconnection coefficient complex;
2. Yoneda or Cech overlap composition;
3. the nonlinear Hull-Strominger defect and its higher derivatives;
4. analytic harmonic-overlap data; or
5. another source-selected coefficient sector.

H4-T8 subsequently closes the universal mechanism in item 3 at the
finite/formal repair tier: the joint jet of the nonlinear residual and its
metric field derives every repair-action vertex. The selected q79 endpoint and
numerical residual/metric jet remain open, as do genuinely different Yoneda,
