## 9. Mathematical context

The use of an odd Hirsch generator whose differential is the Euler class is
the standard commutative-DGA model for an odd spherical, in particular circle,
fibration. K3 formality permits replacement of its de Rham algebra by its
cohomology ring at this rational topological tier. These standard inputs are
used only to identify the model; every finite-dimensional statement above is
then checked exactly by the local verifier.

